argus-tty (1.0.0) focal; urgency=medium

  * Initial public release, prepared for Launchpad PPA distribution
    (ppa:yadavramlaxman/argus-tty).
  * Reset version scheme to 1.0.0 ahead of the open-source release.
  * EMAIL_ENABLED now directly controls systemctl enable/disable of the
    argus-tty-mailer.timer unit, instead of always enabling it regardless
    of whether email notifications are configured.
  * Add a new S3_UPLOAD_ENABLED master switch in config.env, mirroring
    EMAIL_ENABLED: when false, argus-tty-finalize skips S3 upload entirely
    without even checking for the aws CLI or credentials.
  * Add MIT LICENSE and debian/copyright.
  * Add optional Google Authenticator (TOTP) two-factor authentication for
    developer/admin SSH sessions, gated by GOOGLE_2FA_ENABLED in
    config.env. Deployer accounts and LITE_RECORDING_USERS are always
    exempt. New/existing accounts get a TOTP secret auto-provisioned by
    'argus-tty add'/'add-admin', printed once like the generated PEM key.
  * Add DEVELOPER_GROUP_NAME/ADMIN_GROUP_NAME/DEPLOYER_GROUP_NAME in
    config.env, letting an org rename the three tiers. reconfigure safely
    renames an already-populated Linux group in place (groupmod -n) rather
    than orphaning existing accounts, and the CLI gains matching
    add-<term>/bulk-add-<term>s/remove-<term>/list-<term>s aliases
    alongside the existing verbs, which always keep working.
  * Remove all references to the private, unpublished "bosun" package from
    docs, comments, and the shipped defaults — the deployer sudo whitelist
    and related documentation now describe only what argus-tty itself
    enforces, generically.
  * Fix: sshd_config directives outside a Match block use first-occurrence-
    wins, not last. Stock Ubuntu images ship "ChallengeResponseAuthentication
    no" earlier in the file than argus-tty's own managed block, which was
    silently overriding the 2FA feature's override and disabling
    keyboard-interactive authentication entirely — refusing every SSH
    login, including for deployer/LITE_RECORDING_USERS accounts that
    should never even see a prompt. Now neutralized (reversibly) before
    the managed block is appended.
  * Fix: the PAM stack backing the 2FA exemption logic had two bugs found
    via real end-to-end SSH testing: pam_succeed_if's [success=N] jump
    count was hardcoded to 1 regardless of position, which only worked
    with a single exemption condition; and the stack had no terminal
    pam_permit.so for a matched exemption to land on, so a matched
    condition still resulted in a denied login. Both fixed.
  * Fix: debian/rules and debian/conffiles referenced
    /etc/profile.d/developer-restrictions.sh, which is now generated
    dynamically by reconfigure.sh (from the resolved tier group names)
    instead of shipped as a static file — this broke the Launchpad
    (debhelper) build path outright.
  * Fix: lower debhelper-compat from 13 to 12 so the source package
    actually builds on Ubuntu 20.04 "focal" (ships debhelper 12.10, not
    13) — verified by a real build on Ubuntu 20.04/22.04/24.04/26.04.
  * Fix: install.sh's manual-install path referenced non-existent
    sudoers/{developer,admin}.sudoers files (missing the .sample suffix)
    and never installed the deployer sudoers sample, breaking Option C
    (manual, no .deb) installs entirely.

 -- Ram Laxman Yadav <yadavramlaxman@gmail.com>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 18:29:52 +0530
